

Foundation of all Earthly and Cosmic Events


These Laws of Creation, which can also be called Cosmic, Natural or Divine Laws, take up the focal and universal position, for no single event can take place outside them. They form, preserve, regulate and maintain the entire universe down to the minutest happening, which can only be discerned with the help of a microscope.


In reality, they are the recognisable effects to humans of the creative Will of God. As such, they are not at all comparable to human legislation; instead they are omnipresent and self-acting forces which nothing and no one can escape. Since they arise from perfection, they are also perfect and built on an absolute principle and genuine progress for the benefit of all people, animals and nature.


Therefore, there is nothing more natural than to get to know these Laws and to adapt to their peculiarities, to bring oneself into harmony with them, instead of acting against them. In the end, all suffering and disease can be avoided, because in reality health and prosperity would be the normal state, which naturally results from a life in accordance with the Laws of Creation. Illness always occurs as a corrective to draw our attention to wrong attitudes that require change.


But since only a few people know or want to know the three or, in the broader sense, five Natural Laws, no one should be surprised that suffering, hardship and chaos are increasing because of the lack of knowledge and willingness to harmonise with the Natural Order of things.


In contrast to human laws, cosmic laws cannot be circumvented or outwitted! They register our true intentions down to the smallest detail and manifest themselves accordingly, regardless of whether these intentions lead to concrete actions or not. That is why the purification and clarification of our entire inner life and thoughts is far more important than we generally think.


Another important aspect of these Laws is the freedom we wish to grant ourselves. Does freedom mean that we can do whatever we want? Does it mean that we don't have to be accountable to anyone and are not responsible for our misdeeds? Of course not, because freedom is there for everyone and must not be obtained at the expense of others. This, in turn, requires justice, which must be part of a perfect Natural Order.


Here again, the Laws of Creation, to which we are subject every second of our lives, act as guardians of this universal justice. Real freedom, therefore, means that we use their possibilities to our own and others' benefit through wise arrangement.

